title The rune the language wants -- the pair-faces survey ends at a mul gap, and the sameness law holds inside Glow itself
prompt Keaton's kg with Mind restarted and the fleet six-wide; the named door was more Skate desks over the pair-faces grammar for the width-and-height laws.
think The survey answered in two findings and both are worth more than a desk. First, the sameness law held inside Glow: the relational pair-bound gate (gate-tally-garden-pair-bound-u32, STOA340) is vane-neutral by its own header -- two runtime faces, any cap -- so minting a Skate twin of an identical body would be the note_path disease in a new language, and no desk was minted. The claims geometry law (extent within 4096) is already sayable through the existing relational desk. Second, the law the family truly lacks -- lit <= width x height, surface_claims' own no-surface-lights-more-than-it-holds -- CANNOT be said: the gate shop's conditional grammar admits gth and eq alone (glow/rune_shop_gate.rye lines 222-224, read at the source), and no living desk speaks mul. A genuine rune gap, met exactly where the card's law says it lands: an ITINERARY line where Sound's custody answers, the ruling meeting Keaton directly.
think The card takes the Glow rune door (mul in condition operands, or a composed arithmetic face -- the ruling his), pays its bytes from the LOCA paragraph's now-redundant tail, and closes at 24,567 of 24,576. The aether formula turned a third time today -- the canon has returned seven times against a roughly-daily design, so this lap applied the row's listening in one sentence rather than an eighth read: what the work is saying tonight is that the language's own edges are the lane's real frontier, which is precisely what Glow language custody is FOR.
obs The day closes at forty-two session logs on this shelf: the sameness arc, door B and the clean ledger, three walls behind walls, the fleet re-mapped and six-wide with five always-on, the fusion landed, two cross-bench finds fixed within their hours, the first Skate laws in Glow, and a rune ruling set neatly on the sill for morning.
